Word list used by src/listings.rs to tell business names from everyday words.

english-words.fc
  Source: FreeBSD share/dict/web2 (Webster's Second International Dictionary, 1934).
  Licence: public domain. The FreeBSD README for share/dict states: "The 1934 copyright has
  lapsed, according to the supplier."
  Changes: lower-case a-z entries of 3 to 10 letters only, sorted, duplicates removed, and
  front-coded. Rebuild with:
    python3 src/data/build-english-words.py /usr/share/dict/web2 src/data/english-words.fc

The list is used only for membership checks and is never shown to visitors.

The short list of common UK first names in src/listings.rs (FIRST_NAME_LIST) was written for
this project and is covered by the project's MIT licence.

outcode-centroids.csv
  Used by src/postcodes.rs to rank directory listings by distance from a visitor's postcode.
  Source: OS Code-Point Open (CSV, GB), dataset version 2026.3.0 (copyright date 2026-07-20),
  https://www.ordnancesurvey.co.uk/products/code-point-open
  Licence: Open Government Licence v3.0,
  https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
  Attribution:
    Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right 2026.
    Contains Royal Mail data © Royal Mail copyright and database right 2026.
    Contains National Statistics data © Crown copyright and database right 2026.
  Changes: one row per outcode (postcode district), the mean position of its postcodes with
  real coordinates (positional quality below 60), converted from National Grid (OSGB36) to
  WGS84 latitude/longitude (Helmert transformation, about 5 m) and rounded to 4 decimal places.
  Non-geographic districts are left out. Great Britain only: Code-Point Open has no Northern
  Ireland (BT), Channel Islands or Isle of Man postcodes. Rebuild with:
    python3 src/data/build-outcode-centroids.py codepo_gb.zip src/data/outcode-centroids.csv
